eny programmatic access requests from any program.\r\n- Prompt user based on computer security. Outlook will only prompt users when antivirus software is out of date or not running. This is the default configuration.\r\n\r\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, when an untrusted application attempts to use the Save As command, Outlook relies on the setting configured in the ''Programmatic Access'' section of the Trust Center.","categoryId":"a36b9aa4-52d0-44a4-bc2c-eec26d2a53ec","baseUri":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_Security~L_SecurityFormsettings~L_ProgrammaticSettings/L_OOMSaveAs","rootDefinitionId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomsaveas","uxBehavior":"toggle","applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomsaveas_0","options":[{"itemId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomsaveas_0","displayName":"Disabled","dependedOnBy":[]},{"itemId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomsaveas_1","displayName":"Enabled","dependedOnBy":[{"dependedOnBy":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomsaveas_l_oomsaveas_setting","required":true}]}]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationChoiceSettingDefinition","id":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomaddressaccess","name":"L_OOMAddressAccess","displayName":"Configure Outlook object model prompt when reading address information (User) (Deprecated)","description":"This policy setting controls what happens when an untrusted program attempts to gain access to a recipient field, such as the ''To:'' field, using the Outlook object model.\r\n\r\nIf you enable this policy setting,  you can choose from four different options when an untrusted program attempts to access a recipient field using the Outlook object model:\r\n\r\n- Prompt user. The user will be prompted to approve every access attempt.\r\n- Automatically approve. Outlook will automatically grant programmatic access requests from any program. This option can create a significant vulnerability, and is not recommended.\r\n- Automatically deny. Outlook will automatically deny programmatic access requests from any program.\r\n- Prompt user based on computer security. Outlook will only prompt users when antivirus software is out of date or not running. This is the default configuration.\r\n\r\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, when an untrusted application attempts to access recipient fields, Outlook relies on the setting configured in the ''Programmatic Access'' section of the Trust Center.","categoryId":"a36b9aa4-52d0-44a4-bc2c-eec26d2a53ec","baseUri":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_Security~L_SecurityFormsettings~L_ProgrammaticSettings/L_OOMAddressAccess","rootDefinitionId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomaddressaccess","uxBehavior":"toggle","applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomaddressaccess_0","options":[{"itemId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomaddressaccess_0","displayName":"Disabled","dependedOnBy":[]},{"itemId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomaddressaccess_1","displayName":"Enabled","dependedOnBy":[{"dependedOnBy":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_oomaddressaccess_l_oomaddressaccess_setting","required":true}]}]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationChoiceSettingDefinition","id":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_simplemapinameresolve_l_simplemapi_setting","name":"L_SimpleMapi_Setting","displayName":"Guard behavior: (User)","categoryId":"a36b9aa4-52d0-44a4-bc2c-eec26d2a53ec","baseUri":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_Security~L_SecurityFormsettings~L_ProgrammaticSettings/L_SimpleMapiNameResolve","rootDefinitionId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_simplemapinameresolve","uxBehavior":"default","applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_simplemapinameresolve_l_simplemapi_setting_1","options":[{"itemId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_simplemapinameresolve_l_simplemapi_setting_1","displayName":"Prompt User","dependedOnBy":[]},{"itemId":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_outlk16v2~policy~l_microsoftofficeoutlook~l_security~l_securityformsettings~l_programmaticsettings_l_simplemapinameresolve_l_simplemapi_setting_2","displayName":"Automatically Approve",